{"term":"stone","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:fc692b2262bd1a37cd","definition":"A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","example":"Toad, that vnder cold ſtone, / Dayes and Nights ha’s thirty one: / Sweltred Venom ſleeping got, / Boyle thou firſt i’th’ charmed pot.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["rock","rock"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:61bf0918600326bb8d","definition":"A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble.","example":"A railway station which formerly stood a few miles from Sydney has recently been demolished, stone by stone, and has been re-erected as a church in the Australian Capital Territory of Canberra, about 200 miles away.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["pebble"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:15d412f6f2977d1ca5","definition":"A gemstone, a jewel, especially a diamond.","example":"[…]Ineſtimable Stones, vnvalewed Iewels[…]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["hard stone-like deposit"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b6d70a245e161ab839","definition":"A unit of weight equal to 14 pounds (≈6.3503 kilograms), formerly used for various commodities (wool, cheese, etc.), but now principally used for personal weight. Abbreviated as st.","example":"British people mea